      "content": "thanks for this. it looks good. i'm a bit worried about what kind of specific documentation they're gonna ask for though. since these are old family papers and not some digital database entry, what kind of specific \"proof\" should i mention in follow-up communications to make them take the claim seriously? like, should i focus on the signatures or the specific mentions of inheritance in the original charters? i want to sound like i know exactly what legal weight these docs carry.",
